<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul bourse to halt Inkel, Now prior to delisting.</title>
<headline>Seoul bourse to halt Inkel, Now prior to delisting.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Korea Stock Exchange said on Friday it would halt trading in shares of Inkel Corp and Now Precision Co Ltd from October 29 to November 1, when they are scheduled to be delisted.</p>
<p>Haitai Electronics Co Ltd's  plan to absorb its two affiliated firms and become a comprehensive electronics company was approved by investors in July.</p>
<p>After the merger, Haitai's paid-in capital will be increased to 66.77 billion won from 32.68 billion, Haitai said in May. The total number of shares will rise to 13.35 million from 6.54 million.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
